# .gitattributes — the eol contract. Without it, G6 and G25 fail on the Windows cells.
# Specified verbatim in 11-repo-layout.md section 1.9.
*                       text=auto eol=lf
schema/**               text eol=lf
schema/expected/**      -diff
docs/reference/**       text eol=lf
*.owdoc                 binary
*.sql                   text eol=lf
# The NAME is 11-repo-layout.md:473's (this file is section 1.9's artefact); `-diff` is
# 07-store-and-retrieval.md:3141's, whose section 13.2 owns what this file's attributes MEAN.
# 11 section 1.9's subject is the eol=lf contract and it never discusses `-diff`, so omitting
# it there is silence rather than a contrary claim. `-diff` and NOT `binary`: it suppresses
# the DISPLAY (the reviewable diff is `ow store diff`, which speaks documents) and leaves the
# MERGE alone, while `binary` implies `-text` and would forfeit both the eol=lf contract and
# git's default text merge -- the sanctioned, loud fallback for a clone with the attribute and
# no driver. `_plan/_notes/build-defects.md` D20.
omniweave.index.lock    merge=ow-index-lock -diff
